              "value": "Trampling Charge"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "The raised cavalry Strides twice with a +10-foot circumstance bonus to its Speed. During this movement, the cavalry can move through the spaces of Medium or smaller creatures. It deals 3d12+14 bludgeoning damage to each creature whose space it moves through (DC 41 basic Reflex save). A creature that fails its save is also knocked prone. The cavalry can affect the same creature only once in a single use of Trampling Charge."
